    "field": "Sea-level rise",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the challenge of estimating historical global mean sea-level rise using a sparse, geographically biased network of tide gauges, whose significant local variability and data gaps complicate efforts to determine a robust global average trend, particularly before the modern satellite altimeter record.",
    "method": "The authors use a Reduced Space Optimal Interpolation technique, applying spatial patterns (EOFs) from satellite altimeter data to reconstruct historical global mean sea level from sparse coastal and island tide-gauge measurements from 1880 to 2009.",
    "task": "The task is to estimate the rise in global average sea level from 1880 to 2009 by combining data from satellite altimetry with historical coastal and island sea-level measurements.",
